docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md-60-## 5. [ ] Gatekeeper HTTP surface: drain the body on early refusals
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md:61:`harness/gatekeeper.py` `serve()`: the 403 and 413 paths return without reading the
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md-62-request body, so on a keep-alive connection the leftover bytes are parsed as the next
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md-63-request line. Read and discard `Content-Length` bytes (bounded) or send
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md-64-`Connection: close` before returning. Add a test with a raw socket. No other changes.
