docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md:66:## 6. [ ] Merge holds a write transaction across `git merge`
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md:67:`gatekeeper.merge` runs `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` → `set_status` → `git merge` (up to 120s) →
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md:68:`COMMIT`, while `connect()` sets a 15s busy timeout — so a slow merge turns concurrent
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md:69:panel writers into "couldn't finish" skips. Either raise the busy timeout above the merge
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md-70-timeout in `harness/db/jobs.py::connect`, or restructure so git runs outside the
docs/gpt/GPT_TASK_QUEUE.md-71-transaction against a re-checked precondition. Say which and why in the worklog.
