docs/TODO.md-133-### Fix the record layer
docs/TODO.md-134-- [ ] **Tie reviews to a version.** Today: approve version A, builder changes it to B,
docs/TODO.md-135-      **the old approval still counts.** Sol calls this the most dangerous flaw — it
docs/TODO.md-136-      produces *"believable green checks on code nobody reviewed."*
docs/TODO.md-137-- [ ] **A fail must condemn a VERSION, not the job forever.** Right now a fixed build can
docs/TODO.md-138-      never ship.
docs/TODO.md-139-- [ ] **Block DELETING verdicts** (editing fail→pass is blocked; deleting isn't).
docs/TODO.md-140-- [ ] **Reserve budget BEFORE the provider call.** Refusing to *record* a charge doesn't
docs/TODO.md:141:      unspend the money.
docs/TODO.md-142-- [ ] **Agents get NO write access to the safety database.** *"The database cannot be the
docs/TODO.md-143-      jailer if the prisoner can rewrite the jail."*
docs/TODO.md-144-
docs/TODO.md-145-### The missing pieces
docs/TODO.md:146:- [ ] **A trusted gatekeeper service** holding all irreversible powers (merge, deploy,
docs/TODO.md:147:      spend). Agents *ask*; it checks the approval, does exactly that one thing, refuses
docs/TODO.md:148:      everything else. **This is what makes a database permission mean anything.**
docs/TODO.md:149:- [ ] **A hard emergency stop** that doesn't depend on Chief being alive.
docs/TODO.md-150-- [ ] **Separate cancellation** for: the speech, Chief's current thought, queued work, a
docs/TODO.md-151-      running builder. *("No, wait" currently stops the mouth but NOT the work.)*
docs/TODO.md-152-- [ ] **Numbered conversation turns** so an old answer can't arrive after a newer
docs/TODO.md-153-      correction.
docs/TODO.md-154-- [ ] **Duplicate protection** so a retry can't start the same job twice.
docs/TODO.md-155-- [ ] **Crash recovery** — reconcile jobs after sleep, power loss, network failure,
docs/TODO.md-156-      OpenClaw restart.
docs/TODO.md-157-- [ ] **Latency guard.** Chief spiked to 20–35s. A silent car is a failure — hard timeout
