docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-299-#### Open mic is the DEFAULT (confirmed from docs)
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-300-
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-301-- `turn_detection` **defaults to `server_vad`**. **`turn_detection: null` IS push-to-talk** — the
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-302-  opt-out. **Reverting §5.2 is a deletion, not a build.**
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-303-- **Use `semantic_vad` with `eagerness: "low"`** — a classifier that judges whether the speaker
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-304-  actually *sounded finished*. This is the right call for a car: **a driver pauses mid-sentence to
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md:305:  merge, and plain `server_vad` will cut him off.** Semantic VAD is specifically designed not to.
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-306-- **Barge-in is native** — `interrupt_response: true` + `create_response: true`. User speech during
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-307-  assistant playback truncates the assistant's turn.
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-308-
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-309-#### Open-mic cost: a non-issue
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-310-
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-311-Audio is duration-encoded: user audio = **600 tok/min**. Worst case, if silence were billed raw:
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-312-**$0.36/hr (mini)** / $1.15/hr (full). A 45-min drive = **$0.27 on mini.** Rounding error next to the
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-313-conversation itself.
