docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-360-
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-361-- Apple's contract is conditional: the app keeps running in background *"as long as it is recording
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md:362:  audio content."* An idle session gets suspended.
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-363-- **[Apple Forums #776055](https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/776055):** a *shipping* native
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-364-  background-recording app reports a subset of users **routinely get recordings killed** by the
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-365-  watchdog. They stripped the entire view hierarchy on background to get CPU to 0% in the profiler,
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-366-  saw "massive improvements," and **still see background terminations.** Apple publishes **no CPU or
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-367-  memory thresholds** for what survives.
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-368-- **Picovoice's own FAQ hedges:** background wake-word "is controlled by the operating system, and
docs/OSS_RESEARCH_2026-07-11.md-369-  Picovoice **cannot guarantee** that this will be possible in future releases of iOS."
