docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-128-- **Vendor policy drift is the #1 risk.** Anthropic already moved headless to credits; Google killed consumer CLI access; xAI's openness is young. Mitigation: provider abstraction, pinned versions, no single-vendor dependency, text fallback always.
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-129-- **Claude headless = credit pool, always.** Never architect around gray-area workarounds (e.g., puppeting interactive sessions programmatically) — Anthropic bans aggressive circumvention, and the sanctioned path is cheap anyway.
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-130-- **iOS PWA audio quirks** — likeliest engineering pain in Phase 3; prototype early.
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-131-- **Local model overconfidence** — enforce the never-ship-unreviewed rule in the pipeline itself, not by convention.
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-132-- **Token burn** — parallel gauntlets multiply usage; instrument per-provider usage counters from day one and surface them in the UI.
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-133-
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-134-## 10. External connection: Jess (future)
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-135-
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md:136:Jess (Neill's personal assistant, built separately on the Google/Gemini stack in her own project) will connect to this Builder as a **relay over the tailnet** — not a merge. The Builder exposes a small message-in / result-out endpoint; Jess drops build requests onto the Builder's queue and reads results back. "One voice, two brains": Neill talks to Jess, she forwards build tasks to the Builder and relays the answer. No shared substrate, no shared voice pipeline — just a fat tailnet pipe (no HIPAA constraint between these two). Build this endpoint so it's ready when Jess wants it; Jess's own scope lives in her separate spec.
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-137-
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-138-## 11. Out of scope (v1)
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-139-
docs/CC_REBOOT_SPEC_2026-07-11.md-140-Wake word / always-listening; open-mic interruption (barge-in); multi-user access; trillion-parameter local models; any Google integration; home-automation integrations. **Jess's personal-assistant capabilities are explicitly out of scope for this spec** — she is a separate app on a separate stack (§10).

