Two concrete security paths have now survived review: the merge check proves only that one expected output file was reviewed, not that the rest of the commit was reviewed; and the paid builder path checks a ledger but never reserves money before starting the provider call. I’m now checking the committed review transcripts for accidental credential material and validating the approval and network races before ranking everything.
